## Vercel Web Analytics Installation Complete

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Qurator project.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files:**

1. **qurator/src/app/layout.tsx**
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the AuthProvider closing tag
   - Follows Next.js App Router best practices by placing the Analytics component in the root layout

2. **qurator/package.json**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics` version `^2.0.1` to dependencies

3. **qurator/package-lock.json**
   - Updated lockfile with @vercel/analytics and its dependencies (405 packages added)

### Implementation Details

- **Framework**: Next.js 16.2.4 (App Router)
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Analytics Package**: @vercel/analytics@^2.0.1
- **Installation Method**: Following official Vercel documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

The implementation follows the recommended approach for Next.js App Router projects:
- Analytics component imported from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Component placed in root layout (src/app/layout.tsx) within the body tag
- Positioned after all application content for optimal performance

### Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ Package installed successfully using `npm install @vercel/analytics`
2. ✅ Analytics component imported and added to root layout
3. ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`) - no compilation errors
4. ✅ Linter executed (`npm run lint`) - no new errors introduced by our changes
5. ✅ Lock files updated to ensure dependency consistency

### Next Steps for Deployment

To complete the analytics setup:

1. Deploy the project to Vercel using `vercel deploy` or by pushing to your connected Git repository
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project's Analytics section
   - Click the "Enable" button to activate tracking
3. Verify analytics are working:
   - After deployment, visit your live site
   - Open browser DevTools → Network tab
   - Filter for "Fetch/XHR" requests
   - Look for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*` endpoints to confirm tracking is active

### Notes

- All existing functionality preserved
- No breaking changes introduced
- Analytics will only send data when deployed on Vercel
- The implementation is production-ready and follows Vercel's latest best practices
